 "about": "Regular Kham Mueang (Northern Thai) <-> Central Thai mappings to help an LLM normalise Northern speech written in Thai script to standard Thai. Rules are tendencies, not absolute; always prefer glossary lookups first. Northern forms here are as written in Thai script by native-speaker web sources (Chiang Mai / Chiang Rai), whose tone-mark spellings are informal.",
 "how_to_use": [
  "1. Look up whole words/phrases in kham_mueang_glossary.json.",
  "2. Apply lexical substitutions (lexical_map) for high-frequency function words.",
  "3. If still unknown, try reversing the consonant rules (e.g. Northern ฮ- -> Central ร-; Northern unaspirated ก/จ/ต/ป -> Central ค/ช/ท/พ) and check if a real Central word results.",
  "4. Ignore Northern tone marks (๋ ๊) when matching; they encode Northern tones on otherwise identical words (กิ๋น = กิน)."
 ],
